<title>USA: US banks free reserves $1.023 bln Feb 12 rvsd 2 wk.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $1.023 bln Feb 12 rvsd 2 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had revised free reserves of $1.023 billion per day in the two weeks ended February 12, versus revised free reserves of $1.190 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $18 million, unchanged from the prior period. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
